From: edgytoast <146565462+edgytoast@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Window speed: the FIFO's waits in the kernel, the mirror's lists grown geometrically

From the Wind Waker port's 0106. visionOS's libc++ has no native atomic wait (its wait polls,
oversleeping by up to half its wait, up to 64 ms at a time), so on visionOS the FIFO worker and
drain() spin 50 us, then sleep on the address (os_sync_wait_on_address), woken only when they say
they're asleep; AURORA_FIFO_KERNEL_WAIT=0 waits as before. The mirror's merge grows each material's index
list geometrically instead of to the exact size per draw, and its finishing worker runs at
user-interactive QoS.

